 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56200"} "800 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56207"} "1,500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56212"} "5 miles, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56213"} "Marathon, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56214"} "110 metres Hurdles, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56221"} "1,500 metres Race Walk, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56223"} "High Jump, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56224"} "Standing High Jump, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56225"} "Pole Vault, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56226"} "Long Jump, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56233"} "Standing Long Jump, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56238"} "Triple Jump, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56245"} "Shot Put, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56252"} "Stone Throw, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56246"} "Discus Throw, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56249"} "Discus Throw, Greek Style, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56253"} "Javelin Throw, Freestyle, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56256"} "Pentathlon (Ancient), Men"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "57165"} "1920"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/65"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "3,000 metres Race Walk, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} " 2 May 1906"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Intercalated"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/186"} "Panathinaiko Stadio, Athina"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/56222"} "8 from 5 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "After the scandal that had occurred during the " [:a {:href "/results/56221"} "1,500 meter walk"] ", it was suggested to Crown Prince Konstantinos that another walking race should be held on the following day. and that he should take over the job of umpire.  The Crown Prince accepted this suggestion, and a 3,000-meter walking race was added to the programme at the last minute, scheduled for the morning of the last day of the Olympics, shortly before the closing ceremonies.  All the walkers who had competed in the 1,500-meter event were invited to compete in this as well.  However, the first and second place finishers from the 1,500-meter walk, " [:a {:href "/athletes/78127"} "George Bonhag"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/79592"} "Don Linden"] ", did not compete.  The 3,000-meter walk event again developed into a fierce struggle between " [:a {:href "/athletes/79620"} "Robert Wilkinson"] " of Great Britain and " [:a {:href "/athletes/79585"} "Eugen Spiegler"] " of Austria.  Near the finish, as they fought for the title, both increased their speed and broke into a run, and were immediately disqualified by the Crown Prince.  The third place finisher, " [:a {:href "/athletes/79705"} "György Sztantics"] ", crossed the finish line third but became the Olympic champion."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Barcs described Sztantics’ victory thusly, “The Olympic champion was an office worker in the town hall of a small Hungarian town.  After his success the mayor of his town instructed him to act as the host, and entertain all of the athletes in the Zappeion.  Along with the instructions, the money for this arrived by telegram, and the result was that the following day two barrels of Marsala wine were rolled into the quarters of the sportsmen.  It was not very long before shrill singing filled the tremendous hall and the different nationalities were happily mixing.  And in amazing disharmony they sang together.  It is recorded that at about midnight, the Hungarians and Austrians were kissing each other on the cheek, and in those times - as an Olympic feat - this certainly counted as a world record.”"] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "861"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/79705"} "György Sztantics"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "15:13.2"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "436"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/79625"} "Hermann Müller"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "15:20.0"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/79683"} "Georgios Saridakis"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GRE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GRE.png"}] "GRE"]] [:td {} "15:33.0"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "187"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/79646"} "Pantelis Ektoros"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GRE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GRE.png"}] "GRE"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "5"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/79672"} "Ioannis Panagoulopoulos"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GRE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com